  "title": "Use of insurance loss data by local authorities in Norway",
  "summary": "Urban flooding and storm-related losses are rising due to climate change. The insurance industry, through data sharing on extreme weather-related claims, can aid adaptation planning and risk management. This Norwegian pilot project highlights the usefulness of insurance loss data for municipalities. Losses and damages related to urban flooding and storms are likely to increase due to climate change. The insurance industry can potentially play a key role in climate change adaptation by contributing to the understanding of risks associated with climate change.",
